1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,950
Lesson 33: wire antennas, chart and purple buttons

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:19,938
YA-NEC course, lesson 33: the Wire antennas card, the chart and the purple buttons. Calculators, HF family, Wire antennas.

3
00:00:19,988 --> 00:00:33,605
At the top the type: multiband or single band EFHW, with the 49 to 1 or the 64 to 1, or a non-resonant wire with the 9 to 1 or the 4 to 1. The loading coil is optional: it adds a lower band.

4
00:00:33,655 --> 00:00:45,971
The counterpoise: a 0.05 wavelength wire as AA5TB suggests, the coax shield up to the choke, or none. The transformer core carries the losses measured by DG1JAN.

5
00:00:46,021 --> 00:00:57,465
Six layouts: sloping up or down, vertical, inverted L and U, straight. On the right the drawing with the counterpoise.

6
00:00:57,515 --> 00:01:12,477
Below, the boxes: radiating wire, counterpoise, capacitor across the primary, voltage at the end, core, core losses and power.

7
00:01:12,527 --> 00:01:20,877
For each band the SWR through the transformer, from the TF5NN line model. The full check is done by NEC.

8
00:01:20,927 --> 00:01:27,724
Tune the length with NEC looks for the length with the best SWR on all the harmonics, with the counterpoise and the ground.

9
00:01:27,774 --> 00:01:43,680
The Chart button opens tables already computed with NEC: for each lowest band the half wave from the formula, tuned single band, tuned multiband and the quarter wave. The colour goes from green to red with the SWR.

10
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:55,613
At the top you choose the transformer, 49 to 1, 64 to 1 or 9 to 1 with the best lengths or the VE3EED ones, average or perfect ground, with or without counterpoise.

11
00:01:55,663 --> 00:02:13,578
I pick the 40 metre multiband row and press Use this row in the card: the values go into the card, then the calculation is free again.

12
00:02:13,628 --> 00:02:29,045
The purple buttons open another card already filled in. Build the transformer opens Balun and Unun with ratio, frequencies, power and core, and the winding drawing.

13
00:02:29,095 --> 00:02:49,588
Back returns to the wire antennas. Coax choke opens the ferrite toroids with the turns for more than a thousand ohms on the lowest band.

14
00:02:49,638 --> 00:02:55,588
End of lesson 33. Thank you for watching.
